  "text": "\r\n\t\t ELECTION TRAFFIC | Bedford, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     Boards & Commissions   \t\t\t \n     Departments   \t\t\t \n     Community   \t\t\t \n     Business   \t\t\t \n     How Do I...   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \nStay Informed \nGet news and updates sent right to your phone or inbox! \r\n\t\t\t Sign up for Notifications \r\n\t\t\t Voter Registration \r\n\t\t\t\t Application Information \r\n\t\t\t\t Determining Applicant Qualifications \r\n\t\t\t Filing for Office \r\n\t\t\t Candidates for Office \r\n\t\t\t ELECTION TRAFFIC \r\n\t\t\t Town Moderator Announcements \r\n\t\t\t Public Notice - Electronic Ballot Counting Device Testing \r\n\t\t\t Public Notice - Ballot Counting \r\n\t\t\t Legal Notice Protest Petition \r\nHome \nDepartments \nDepartments \nTown Clerk \nElection Information \nELECTION TRAFFIC \r\nELECTION TRAFFIC\t\t \r\nENTERING AND EXITING BEDFORD HIGH SCHOOL \nTraffic at the intersection of County Road and Nashua Road is being redirected to create a continuous traffic flow into and out of the campus.   \nVoters will only be able to access the voting from Nashua Road south from Route 101 in which they take a right turn  only  onto campus, or from County Road westbound onto campus. \nDuring voting, there will be no left turns allowed from Nashua Road onto County Road .  Also, there will be  no left turns from County Road onto Nashua Road.   All northbound traffic on Nashua Road will be stopped near the area of 54 Nashua Road. \nLeaving the school, vehicles will only be allowed to go straight across onto County Road or a right turn onto Nashua Road. \r\nSCHOOL TRAFFIC FLOW \nCars will find parking in a counterclockwise manner and be assisted by members of the Bedford Police Department and Bedford CERT.  All traffic will have to take the first right after entering the school and then take the parking lot of their choice.  Handicap parking is adjacent to the gymnasium entrance.   \nAfter voting, vehicles will exit in a counterclockwise fashion and off campus by travelling east on County Road or south on Nashua Road.   \r\nSURROUNDING ROADS TRAFFIC FLOW \nLocal traffic and residents on Nashua Road between Wallace Road and County Road should detour via Wallace Road or Gage Road.  \r\n\t\t\t Agendas & \nMeetings \r\n\t\t\t Maps & \nProperty \nInformation \r\n\t\t\t Online \nPayments \r\n\t\t\t Transfer \nStation & \nRecycling \r\n\t\t\t Licenses \n& Permits \r\n\t\t\t Job \nOpenings \r\nContact Us \r\nBedford Town Offices \r\n24 North Amherst Road \r\nBedford, NH 03110 \nPhone:  603-472-5242 \r\nStaff Directory \r\nTown Offices Hours \r\nMonday through Friday: \n8 am to 4:30 pm \nTuesday: \n7 am to 4:30 pm \r\nTransfer Station Hours \r\nSunday and Monday: \nClosed \nTuesday: \n7 am to 5 pm \nWednesday and Friday: \n8:30 am to 5 pm \nThursday: \n8:30 am to 7 pm \nSaturday: \n6:30 am to 3 pm \r\n         Home \n         Site Map \n         Government Websites by CivicPlus® \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
